From 8bc453dac612b76cd308b1191c3cbb6ea072831c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LGNative <luis@nativestride.io>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 20:35:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 30/30] TR importer: drop dead analyzeSecurities block; strict
 ISIN validation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Audit cleanup (no behavior change to resolution):
- Remove the unused analyzeSecurities / SecurityAnalysis / AnalyzedTrade block
  (~135 lines) from tr-isin-tickers.ts — the old 'Unmapped securities' panel was
  removed in the 2-tab simplification; zero callers repo-wide.
- looksLikeIsin now uses the (previously dead) Luhn validator isValidIsin
  instead of the loose /[A-Z]{2}[A-Z0-9]{10}/ regex, which matched words like
  'SUBSCRIPTION' and minted a fake unpriceable asset.

Kept tr-isin-tickers' curated ISIN->listing table: it is the primary resolver
and guards ADR/ratio traps (Alibaba 9988 8:1, Sibanye SSW 4:1, Novo 0.5x) that
the dynamic searchTicker path cannot detect.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
